// Solution to 5.2: one leaf stops being taken on faith.
//
// `graceful` claimed the test dataset was trustworthy and left it there. refine drops the
// whole `trustworthy` argument into that hole. The hook names the element in the *base*
// that gets replaced, and the result has to carry a new name: a model cannot refine
// itself into its own name.
//
// Everything else about graceful is untouched. The conclusion, the severe-error strategy
// and the model leaf are exactly as their author wrote them.

load "../bricks/graceful.jd"
load "../bricks/trustworthy.jd"

justification graceful_deep is refine(graceful, trustworthy) {
    hook: "test_ds"
}
